WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.000
Your coding agent says it's done.

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:09.321
One developer writes that the bottleneck isn't building anymore. It's completing.

3
00:00:09.871 --> 00:00:15.474
One Hacker News post puts it plainly: instructions are not guarantees.

4
00:00:16.024 --> 00:00:21.270
Product Actualizer keeps one model of what is true about your product.

5
00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:26.448
Every claim carries a grade, and a source anyone can re-open.

6
00:00:26.998 --> 00:00:31.251
Public copy may cite only what was observed or verified.

7
00:00:31.251 --> 00:00:35.366
Downgrade a claim, and the validator refuses the page.

8
00:00:35.916 --> 00:00:42.414
Change the model, and whatever cites it goes stale. By version, not by memory.

9
00:00:42.964 --> 00:00:51.013
The work is split into lenses, ordered by what each one needs. The tools that do it are replaceable.

10
00:00:51.563 --> 00:00:57.063
An agent can report work as ready for review. Only the owner can accept it.

11
00:00:57.613 --> 00:01:03.780
And the gate can say no. It will not let the run end while work is outstanding.

12
00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:09.413
Product Actualizer. Finish the product. Show the evidence.
